      "basis": "per (context, seed) gradient of D's objective at E, split by path: F = lambda Z + beta K through the student query (the future), A = A_tf through the teacher-future read (the action); contexts = the first 4 training batches (40); per-tensor Gram matrices of the 160 vectors; the batch-1 in-batch first-order decrease must reproduce step.json's predicted_per_eta"
    },
    "reading": {
      "seed_retained": "rho = (1 - r1) / (1 - r0) on C80 future NMSE, r = arm / E at seed index 0 (the trained trajectories) and 1 (same contexts, unseen noise)",
      "context_rho_min": 0.5,
      "noise_rho_max": 0.25,
      "first_order": "T_seed, T_ctx = mean first-order decrease of the future-path loss (F) from one training step on a batch, on the same contexts at seed 1 and on the other 30 contexts at seed 0, over that on the batch itself; mean over the 4 batches",
      "shared_min": 0.2,
      "next": "context-attached (rho >= 0.5) with T_ctx < 0.2: each context's repair is its own, so more calibration contexts or a parametrization restricted to shared directions; noise-attached (rho <= 0.25): the objective fits one denoising trajectory, so average over sampler seeds or train on a per-step teacher-forced objective"
    },
